The  driver is the backend part of the PCI pass‐through function‐
ality that can be used by the dom0 to export devices to  a  guest
domain.  To export a PCI device to a guest domain, the device has
to  be attached to in the dom0.  When the guest domain is the de‐
vice attached to the driver will attach to a bus inside the guest
domain.  To attach a device to the driver,  follow  these  steps:
look  for  the  device PCI ID, via edit and add the PCI ID to the
list of PCI IDs that you want to attach to in bus:device.function
notation.  The list is passed to dom0 module via  the  parameter:
See  also reboot dom0.  add the PCI ID to the list of PCI devices
in the domain configuration file: start the  guest  domain.   The
driver  first appeared in The driver was written by Currently, to
attach a device to the backend, this procedure  has  to  be  per‐
formed  at  time.   In  the  future, it will be possible to do it
without requiring a dom0 reboot.  As PCI passthrough  offers  the
possibility for guest domains to send arbitrary PCI commands to a
physical  device, this has direct impact on the overall stability
and security of the system.  For example, in case of erroneous or
malicious commands, the device could  overwrite  physical  memory
portions, via DMA.
